  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Creating an Enabling Environment for Adolescent Girls in Egypt</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Egypt):  USAID is supporting a comprehensive effort to eliminate female genital mutilation/cutting (FGM/C) in Egypt. The Creating an Enabling Environment for Adolescent Girls in Egypt activity focuses on the protection and development needs of adolescent girls and supports the Egyptian government&apos;s efforts to combat FGM/C through an integrated set of interventions designed to change perceptions of girls&apos; roles in the family and society while improving the enforcement and reform of FGM/C laws. This activity promotes community dialogue through youth centers, sporting events, and discussions around girls&apos; empowerment. Moreover, it works directly with policymakers to review laws and policies and disseminate best practices from other countries related to FGM/C. While strengthening Egypt&apos;s policy and legal frameworks, this activity is also improving child protection mechanisms by enhancing the capacity of prosecutors, lawyers, social workers, medical providers, and community volunteers to address FGM/C..</narrative>
  </description>
